Design references (no code copied):
- Obsidian — local Markdown vault as the source of truth
- TickTick — task (todo) workflow, imported read-only through a review queue
- By project rule, code of AGPL-licensed projects is never copied; only
  structure and patterns are studied.

Third-party components used as dependencies (not modified):
- BlockNote (@blocknote/core, @blocknote/react, @blocknote/mantine) - MPL-2.0.
  Source: https://github.com/TypeCellOS/BlockNote
- Excalidraw (@excalidraw/*) - MIT
- lightningcss (build tool) - MPL-2.0; Rust crates cssparser, cssparser-macros,
  selectors, dtoa-short, option-ext and others pulled in by Tauri - MPL-2.0
- dompurify - MPL-2.0 OR Apache-2.0 (used under Apache-2.0)
- caniuse-lite (build data) - CC-BY-4.0, attribution: Alexis Deveria and
  contributors
- sqlite-vec - MIT OR Apache-2.0; Playwright - Apache-2.0
- Some Rust crates (for example r-efi) are offered under MIT, Apache-2.0 or
  LGPL-2.1-or-later; the MIT or Apache-2.0 option is used.

Source locations of the unmodified MPL-2.0 components (MPL-2.0 section 3.2 asks
that recipients of executable forms be told where the source is):
- BlockNote: https://github.com/TypeCellOS/BlockNote
- lightningcss: https://www.npmjs.com/package/lightningcss
- Rust crates: https://crates.io/crates/cssparser,
  https://crates.io/crates/cssparser-macros, https://crates.io/crates/selectors,
  https://crates.io/crates/dtoa-short, https://crates.io/crates/option-ext
